WEBVTT

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.150
Morning.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.290
You're always here so early.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.410
I worked overtime, and I'm still not done.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.660
<b>New Area Project</b>

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.870
The species list isn't set yet.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.220
And I haven't finished 
the schedule chart, either.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.680
I have to write a compensation report, too.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.350
Jeez.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.420
That new area project has you swamped.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.970
Why me?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.520
It would have gone more smoothly 
if he'd picked someone more capable, like you!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.760
It's an opportunity.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.470
Try to learn from it.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.150
No, I just know the assistant
director is messing with me.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.690
He's having fun working
a newbie to the bone.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:54.950
Plankton.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.300
Here he comes.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.700
The supply list?

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.230
I'm making it now.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.740
The suppliers want it immediately.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.960
Finish it now.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.590
I need more time.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.490
I asked you three days ago.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.420
I have my hands full already.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.680
Time's ticking by 
while you're making excuses.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.460
Fine, fine, I'll do it!

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.220
That's all you want, right?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.840
Plankton.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.880
What?

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.270
Just say, "Yes, sir."

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.980
Yes, <i>sir</i>!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.670
Lucky.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.020
I wish I were a fish.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.380
What are you up to, Kukuru?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.130
Assimilating life force.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:27.890
What?

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.410
I've been too busy lately 
to hang out with the animals.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.430
You attendants are so lucky.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:39.070
You always get to be with the animals.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.520
That's true.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.120
And you take it for granted, don't you?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.120
You won't realize how important they are 
to you until they're gone!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.000
Sure, sure.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.710
Just say, "Yes, sir."

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.580
Huh?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.990
Are you done over there?

00:03:58.990 --> 00:03:59.740
Eh?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.220
Oh, yeah.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:05.960
There's a wild dolphin that's gotten lost 
around here, apparently.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.950
Umi-yan's going to go check it out. 
Take his spot for me.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.140
I want to go, too!

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.230
No way. No way.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:19.110
Kuuya-san, you knew this was going 
to happen, didn't you?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.540
She never grows.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.620
Are you sure you should be here?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.410
This is a big deal. 
I can't just sit around.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.670
I'll take a quick look 
and then go back.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.040
All right.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.140
Gramps.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:45.960
Hey.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.220
Hard at work, huh?

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.580
Why are you here?

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.920
My pupil from way back 
works for the city.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.350
He wanted me to come take a look.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.480
We were asked to come, too.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.250
It's encouraging to have you here.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.430
Is it here?

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.390
Yeah.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.520
Over there.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.870
Looks like it's just a calf.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.600
Must have gotten separated 
from its pod.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.620
Oh, dear.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.990
It should be with its mother 
at that age.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.460
The mother may have died.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.010
It looks like it's injured.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.850
It seems to be in good shape.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:40.480
Hopefully, it finds its way back 
to open waters.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:48.720
How about we keep an eye on it 
for a while and try not to disturb it?

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.790
All right.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.610
We'll get our staff to come
check on it every now and then.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.620
Okay, thanks.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:08.280
Well, Kukuru, you should come
see Gama Gama when you have some time.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.510
Why?

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.840
It's going to be demolished soon.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.230
You should get a look 
before it's all gone.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.610
It's finally happening, huh?

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.810
Yeah.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:32.170
Just as life returns to the sea, 
we have to see Gama Gama back into the earth.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.710
It's just a kid still.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:46.940
Yeah.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.240
They're going to keep
an eye on it for a while, right?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.380
I'm going to make time 
to see it every day.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.930
Are you sure?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.120
Why not?

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.180
I thought you were busy.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.690
You were at work early this morning, too.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.950
I'm not used to writing up documents.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.820
It takes me so much time.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.280
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.460
I'm going to go take a look 
before work tomorrow.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:13.480
Want to come along?

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:14.700
I do!

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:28.800
There!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.480
Did you see that?

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.800
It just jumped!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.010
It's so cute.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.690
This is so healing.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.230
Ban-chan.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.340
"Ban"?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.260
Ban-chan, because it's a bottlenose dolphin.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:55.070
It must be lonely, suddenly being left 
on its own, even though it's so small.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.010
I was the same way, so I get it.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.720
It's all right, Ban-chan.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.710
We're with you.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:06.100
I hope you get back to your buddies soon.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.180
I'll be back, Ban-chan.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:33.880
Akari-chan, I'm going to go eat outside 
and stop by our business partner.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:34.520
Huh?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.410
Our business partner?

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:37.720
Yeah.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:38.580
Y'know.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.260
Okay, got it.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.730
Look, it's a dolphin!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.500
Oh, wow!

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.800
That dolphin's just a child.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.820
You might scare it if you make a fuss.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.180
Try to watch quietly from a distance.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.980
Okay, got it.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.530
Misakino-kun!

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.490
I heard you went to check 
on the dolphin for us.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.520
The attendants were supposed to go, 
but we just couldn't find the time.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.000
Thanks a lot.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.830
Plankton.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.130
Yes, sir!

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.540
What is this about?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.840
No, um...

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:34.400
Did you not tell the assistant director?

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.180
Oh, man, that's not good.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.760
I just went to check on it 
while I was out.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.640
Is that your job?

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:44.940
No.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.450
You aren't even up to snuff 
on your own work yet.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.650
Don't go meddling in other people's business.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.450
Come on.

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:55.900
She simply did the right thing 
as a member of the aquarium staff.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.260
Right?

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:01.410
It's always the people who can't
do their work that go on about lofty ideals.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.330
What's that? Are you talking about me?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.080
I'm just talking in general.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.960
That was kinda nasty.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.400
I apologize.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.800
I'll leave the dolphin 
to the attendants going forward.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.220
I just want to see results.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.100
The assistant director and the chief?

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.850
They really don't seem to like each other!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.190
They have different ideas 
about how work should be.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.110
It's so fun watching them.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.690
Isn't it fun when there's friction at work?

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.200
You're surprisingly evil, Akari-chan.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.320
Am I busted?

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.940
We might be comrades.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.450
Watching Ban-chan helped me de-stress.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.500
The attendants are going to take turns 
keeping an eye on it.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.040
Don't worry.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.420
Why don't you try focusing 
on your work for once, Kukuru?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.680
You won't learn to enjoy work 
if you never take it seriously.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:16.530
Oh, yeah... I heard from Umi-yan 
that Airi-chan's coming to Tingarla next Friday.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.440
Really?

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:22.080
She's still in physical therapy, 
but she's doing well.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.910
She said she misses us.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.090
She's looking forward to seeing us again.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.040
Yeah?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.290
I can't wait to see her.

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:38.870
I have to show her 
that I'm doing better at work.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:43.050
<b>Lost Plankton</b>

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.380
Plankton.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:05.740
Yes, sir?

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:12.210
We're thinking of making the new area available 
as a wedding venue when it opens.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.130
Weddings at an aquarium?

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.940
It's to create buzz for our new opening.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.050
It'll improve our image.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.560
Prepare a plan on your end.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.840
Yes, sir.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.970
What will I need for it?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:34.080
Put together a sample plan based
on what other aquariums have done.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.060
We'll present it to a wedding
planning company next week.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.080
A presentation?

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.150
If it works out,

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.950
the new area will receive attention 
and increase customer growth dramatically.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.440
This is your chance to show off your skills 
as a project planner.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:49.930
Understood.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.710
<b>aquarium wedding</b>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>How to Plan An Aquarium Wedding 
| Marimbales Sea of Stars</b>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>Aquamarriage | Shirohane Aquarium</b>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>Why Aquarium Weddings Are Great! 
Ceremonies And Photo Plans...</b>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>Top 10 Best Aquariums For Weddings</b>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>What Will Make Your Wedding 
At Hinode Sunahama Aquarium Special</b>

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:09.640
<b>New Area Aquarium Wedding 
Project Proposal (Tentative)</b>

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.500
Overtime again?

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.450
You can head home first, Fuuka.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.040
It must be rough, 
being at work late every day.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:32.940
Yeah.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:34.170
I guess.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:36.040
But there's no one else to do it.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.830
So I have to.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:39.980
There you are!

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.760
Misakino-kun.

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.310
Chief Garandou.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:46.920
So about that lost dolphin...

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.120
It doesn't look as though 
it's leaving any time soon,

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:55.140
so I figure we should swim nearby 
and check on its health.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:56.640
Uh-huh.

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:58.060
Wanna do it?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:03.320
You've been a great help 
to the attendants.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.070
The assistant director won't have anything to say

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.860
if you do it on your own time 
outside work, right?

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.340
What's wrong?

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.990
No, I...

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.000
What? You won't do it?

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:18.590
I have an important presentation to do.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:19.600
Aw, man.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.200
That's too bad.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.620
I'll ask someone else.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:24.120
Don't worry about it.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.200
I'm sure your presentation 
will turn out well.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.840
You've worked so hard on it.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.810
I'm going to go finish the proposal.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.690
It's been a while.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.130
How's Tingarla going?

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.420
It's been doing well.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.070
Thank you for all your advice.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.880
How have you been?

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.460
I miss the animals.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:56.970
The dolphin?

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.300
It's still there.

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:02.780
It seems to have plenty to eat, so we're trying 
not to interfere with it too much.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.670
That's for the best.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.710
There you are.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.500
You aren't drunk yet, huh?

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.760
Tsukimi's not here, so I have to work.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.900
It's so exhausting!

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:18.400
How is everyone from Gama Gama doing?

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.960
They're all very adaptable.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.850
I feel safe with them.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:26.730
Kukuru-san's working as hard 
as she can for us in marketing, too.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:32.740
That girl's practically been swimming 
in a tank her whole life.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:37.090
It'll be a good experience for her 
to see what's outside.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:41.750
I hope she'll become a great aquarist 
just like you someday.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.450
Even if she's barely able 
to float right now.

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:58.010
Are you all right?

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.530
Yes.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:02.640
I put up with a lot for this day.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.420
Nice to meet you.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.910
I'm Miura, a wedding planner.

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:17.610
Thank you for your time today.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:18.510
Not at all.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:21.290
This would be a good opportunity 
for us as well.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:25.670
We produce bespoke weddings here.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:34.630
We have some couples who are interested 
in aquarium weddings.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:38.600
So we're very keen on this.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.830
We look forward to working with you.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.040
This is our proposal for Tingarla Weddings.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.690
<b>Tingarla Weddings</b>

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.690
<b>Proposal</b>

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.810
Thank you.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:53.320
I see.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:58.060
Our plan is to make the new area available 
for weddings, when it opens in the spring.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.600
We'll also be able to hold
mini-receptions at the restaurant,

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:03.980
as part of the special opening event.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.440
May I ask a few questions?

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.170
Yes.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:11.880
"No photography or additional lighting 
in front of tanks."

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:13.340
Does that include during the ceremony?

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.380
Yes.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.490
For the welfare of the fish.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:21.060
Strong flashes will surprise the fish 
that aren't accustomed to them.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.850
What about wedding photos?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:26.230
Would you be preparing a separate location?

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.320
We'll make some considerations.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.930
"Minimal decorations"?

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:34.920
Yes.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:39.570
It can be fatal for fish 
if they mistake decorations for food.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:44.580
So then, with adequate management, 
we can have decorations, correct?

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:46.750
Um...

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.080
I'll get back to you on that.

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:52.460
"We'll serve delicious fish 
at the mini-reception"?

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:53.560
Yes.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:57.640
We think it'll be a good opportunity 
to have people talk about fish.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.280
Do you have a specific kind 
of fish in mind?

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.460
Japanese style? Western style?

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:05.300
Are there special menus for the receptions?

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.230
Menus...

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.480
We haven't considered that yet.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.140
I'm sorry.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:20.740
I understand that Tingarla 
takes good care of its fish.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:26.420
But I don't think we'll find many customers 
who will want this program.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:31.130
A wedding is one of the biggest
moments of someone's life.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:35.890
The fish have to take more 
of a backseat role.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.420
Backseat role...

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:41.550
Could we at least relax 
some of the conditions?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:45.310
The aquariums in the mainland 
allow for more extravagant performances.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:49.560
But if you're holding a wedding at Tingarla, 
the fish have to be the most...

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:56.570
I'm sure a fish getting married
at Tingarla would find real happiness.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.750
Misakino, enough.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:05.110
Thank you for your valuable feedback.

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:09.110
We'll revise the proposal 
and get back to you when we're ready.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.710
I was expecting that reaction.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:19.170
Now that we know what they value, 
we know what we have to do.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:22.260
Redo the plan.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:24.940
Yes, sir.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:30.070
Her opinion is as to be expected 
of a wedding planner.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.850
Rethink it from the ground up.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.160
<b>Morning!
Good luck on your presentation!</b>

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.280
<b>Thanks! I'll do my best.</b>

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.680
<b>I did the dive today 
to check on the dolphin.</b>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
<b>Teruya Tsukimi</b>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
Thanks for today! See you soon!

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
<b>Miyazawa Fuuka</b>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
Sent a photo

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
<b>Kudaka Karin</b>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.000
Is your presentation finished?

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.000
<b>Okay!
I think I'll be all right.</b>

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.000
<b>Airi-chan's here!</b>

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.000
<b>Is your presentation finished?</b>

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.270
That was today!

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.800
Where's Airi-chan?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.510
She said she'll be back.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:10.040
And she asked me to say "hi" to you.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.900
I feel bad.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.030
It's not your fault.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.400
You had work.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.040
Work...

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:45.540
Why was I trying so hard again?

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.220
<b>Wildlife of Kuroshio</b>

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.730
<b>Gama Gama</b>
